  "description": "The proposal includes constructing a traditionally styled open porch (240 cm x 117 cm x 320 cm) to replace the deteriorating non-original porch, reinstating a low London stock brick boundary wall with heritage railings, and enhancing the frontage with greenery and a new Edwardian-style tiled pathway. A secure, low-profile bike storage unit (220 cm x 105 cm x 134 cm) will be discreetly installed, ensuring minimal visual impact. All works have been designed to complement the Aldersbrook Conservation Area’s character and guidelines.\n\n",
